{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"MapLibre Native iOS provides a set of built-in gesture recognizers. You can customize or supplement these gestures according to your use case. You see what gesture recognizers are on your "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by accessing the "},{"code":"gestureRecognizers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property on your map."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Configuring user interaction","anchor":"Configuring-user-interaction"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Several properties on an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" provide ways to enable or disable a set of gesture recognizers. Boolean values are set to "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by default."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapView\/zoomEnabled","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" - Allows the user to zoom in or out by pinching two fingers, double-tapping, tapping with two fingers, or double-tapping then dragging vertically. Accepts Boolean values."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapView\/scrollEnabled","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" - Allows the user to scroll by dragging or swiping one finger. Accepts Boolean values."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapView\/rotateEnabled","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" - Allows the user to rot